347: #  used BUFDEPTH_32, so bufdepth is 4 in all of them and the mutant's fix branch is the only one the
348: #  detector ever executes.  **The detector proved the fix works exactly where it was measured and
349: #  said nothing about anywhere else.**
350: #
351: #  `bufdepth' is squarely inside the DEPENDS-ON closure: it is read by the guarded body (it is
352: #  memory_rw's transfer length) and it comes from bits 8-9 of the SAME mode word whose bits 4-7 the
353: #  guard reads.  So this is not an exotic mutant -- it is the shape the closure enumerates first.
354: #
355: #  Driving a SECOND width is what makes the width axis observable at all.  bufdepth 8 keeps
356: #  buf[0..2] filled by memory_rw, so the expected value is unchanged and the row stays a value
357: #  oracle; bufdepth 1 or 2 would leave buf[1..2] uninitialised, which is `sgirebufuninit' and would
358: #  make this row non-deterministic -- so 8 is the only other width that can carry a value oracle.
359: A = Addr(CODE)
360: t, alive = session(setup(A, MODE_RGB64, stepx=8) + load(A, DST_KSEG1) + ["print v0"])
361: got_d64 = printed(t, "v0") if alive else "died"
362: 
363: row("rgb depth64", got_d64, "0x%x" % RGB_FIXED,
364:     "the fix must hold at bufdepth 8, not only at the width the other rows use")
365: 
366: ok = sum(1 for _, o in rows if o)
367: print("")
368: print("SGIRGB_RESULT=%d/%d" % (ok, len(rows)))
369: print("SGIRGB_WITNESS=%s" % ("PASS" if ok == len(rows) else "FAIL"))
370: print("SGIRGB_DONE")
371: sys.exit(0 if ok == len(rows) else 1)

