codex
My disposition is to defer activation and give the buffer defect a helper-wide fix. The `rgb depth64` row reads eight bytes but writes only four, so it cannot detect an eight-byte PUT’s uninitialised tail. Initialising the buffer and correcting MTE copy semantics therefore need separate closure claims.
